      },
      {
        "name": "The Estimate Is Not Measurement Rule",
        "body": "Past snowfall is model estimate and renders in Ash Faint at 70% opacity; forecast renders in Powder Cyan. The two must never share a color, and each carries a text label (\"model estimate\", \"forecast\").",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint, Don't Fill Rule",
        "body": "Status surfaces use the status hue at 10% fill with a 40–50% border (`warn/10` + `warn/40`, `down/10` + `down/40`). Solid status fills are not used.",
